WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.450
A few more precise phrases.

2
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.525
Length and breadth mean length overall and greatest breadth.

3
00:00:06.775 --> 00:00:08.625
Nothing fancy.

4
00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:14.375
In sight of one another means one vessel can actually be seen visually from the other.

5
00:00:14.625 --> 00:00:16.750
Eyes, not electronics.

6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:25.750
Restricted visibility means visibility reduced by fog, mist, falling snow, heavy rain, sandstorms or anything similar.

7
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.025
Notice what’s not on that list: darkness.

8
00:00:29.275 --> 00:00:32.500
A clear night is not restricted visibility.

9
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.250
And here’s the one that catches people.

10
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:41.900
If you see a target on your radar or AIS in thick fog, you are not in sight of that vessel.

11
00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:48.125
That single fact decides which steering rules apply, and we’ll lean on it heavily in lesson eight.
